{
  "description": "Shared test vectors for 'which legal entities does this person cover for accounting:read and accounting:manage' (specs/20261119-accounting, plan R12). Owned by auth (T2); read by auth's tests (src/authz/derivedApps.test.ts) and, read-only, by accounting-api's coverage.ts tests (T6) and refund-api's accountingViewer.ts tests (T19), so that the two derivations of 'covers an entity' cannot drift.",
  "contract": [
    "A case is: the person's effective permissions (the wire shape of GET /authz/me `permissions`), the user's own entity (null when none), and the expected result.",
    "entities: the only two legal entities are 'welld_ch' and 'welld_it'. A user entity outside them (or null) is covered only by an unconditioned grant.",
    "An unconditioned grant (conditions null) covers both entities, whatever the user's entity.",
    "{attributes:[{key:'entity',match:'user'}]} (and nothing else) covers the user's own entity, and only when the user's entity is one of the two. A null user entity covers nothing.",
    "Any other condition covers nothing (fail closed), and does not hide a recognised grant next to it. The user's entity is compared exactly, case-sensitively.",
    "Only (resource 'accounting', action 'read' or 'manage') count. Every other resource or action is ignored.",
    "covered.read: the entities covered by accounting:read OR accounting:manage (manage includes read, AC-3.2). covered.manage: the entities covered by accounting:manage alone.",
    "appReachable: whether the derived `accounting` entry of /authz/me `apps` is present. It is true exactly when covered.read is not empty (AC-8.1).",
    "Arrays are SETS: compare without regard to order (auth lists entities in its own order, accounting-api in its own)."
  ],
  "entities": [
    "welld_ch",
    "welld_it"
  ],
